{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-gx:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-gx:a432b82c302d1c90c04c920bdb2d713099ddd544153c02688536f7db6704af7f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:27:30Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-gr.land","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-gx","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-gx","title":"bob periods brief -f md prints an empty dates segment on week Parts and raw block ids in no-linked-minutes aliases","status":"open","issue_type":"task","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-04T03:27:30Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-gr.land","updated_at":"2026-11-04T03:27:30Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"","design":"","model":"","size":"small","task_type":"bug","task_type_fields":{"impact":"Cosmetic: the brief and links pasted from it look broken, and an alias can end in a truncated block id.","location":"src/native/periods/brief.rs render_part, still_open_section","repro":"Two Markdown rendering glitches in `bob periods brief`:\n1. `bob periods brief 2026-W41 -f md` (also W42 and W32) prints week Part lines with an empty dates segment, e.g. `- Mon Oct 5 ·  · 2h 55m · …`. `render_part` always formats `label · dates · worked`. Skip the dates segment when it is empty (bob-cli-gr.3 note #2).\n2. `bob periods brief 2026-W30 -f md`, Still open \"No linked minutes\", prints `[[bob#^better-obsidian-image|Better Obsidian image support! ^better-obsidian-image]]` and cuts `^g-highlight…` mid-id. `still_open_section` builds that alias from `short_description(&task.text, 120)` on the raw freshness-scan text. Every other section uses `task_link` with the cleaned `IndexedTask.description`. Strip the block id and inline fields the same way `clean_task_text` does (bob-cli-gr.14 note #1).\n"},"is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"bob-cli-gr.3 and bob-cli-gr.14 found these cosmetic Markdown-rendering defects while drafting the W41 and W30 Reviews. Both are small, local fixes in brief.rs.","dependencies":[]}}}
